from pathlib import Path
from runpy import run_path
g=run_path(str(Path(__file__).with_name('author-tools-generator.py')))
L=g['lesson']; C=g['course']

nginx=[
('Serving a static file','Nginx is a web server. It can answer a request by sending a file, such as index.html, without running a custom application backend.','Request: GET /index.html\nNginx reads: the configured index.html file\nResponse: HTML for the browser','The browser then reads the HTML and may ask for CSS or images too.','Draw the requests needed for a page with one stylesheet.','Serving files is different from executing browser JavaScript on the server.','Who runs the page\'s browser JavaScript?','The browser','Nginx automatically'),
('Read the configuration structure','Nginx configuration uses directives and blocks. Some directives are valid only in specific contexts.','events {}\nhttp {\n  server {\n    listen 127.0.0.1:8080;\n  }\n}','The server block sits inside http. The listen directive binds the practice server to localhost port 8080.','Point to the semicolons and matching braces.','A directive in the wrong context can make configuration validation fail.','Where is this server block placed?','Inside http','Inside a CSS rule'),
('Document roots','root chooses the base directory used to find a requested file. The request path is normally added to that base.','server {\n  listen 127.0.0.1:8080;\n  root /absolute/path/to/club-site;\n}','A request for /style.css points to /absolute/path/to/club-site/style.css. Replace this illustrative path only in a private practice configuration.','Map /images/logo.png to its full file path.','Do not serve a directory containing passwords or private project files.','What file does /style.css select?','style.css under the configured root','Any style.css on the computer'),
('Index documents','index names files to try when a request refers to a directory. index.html is a common first page.','location / {\n  index index.html;\n}','A request for a directory can use its index.html. The file must actually exist and be readable.','Explain what should happen if the index file is missing.','An index directive does not create the file.','What does index index.html name?','A default directory page','A database index'),
('Locations match request paths','A location block chooses handling for matching request paths. Simple prefix locations are useful for organising a static site.','location /assets/ {\n  root /absolute/path/to/club-site;\n}','The prefix matches paths beginning with /assets/. With root, the assets part stays in the resulting path.','Map /assets/logo.png to the full path.','root and alias combine paths differently; do not interchange them without checking.','Does root keep /assets/ in this file path?','Yes','No'),
('Check files with try_files','try_files checks candidate paths and uses a final fallback when none exists. Static generated pages often need directory index handling.','location / {\n  try_files $uri $uri/ =404;\n}','Nginx tries a file, then a directory. If neither exists, it returns status 404.','Trace requests for an existing CSS file and a missing page.','Do not rewrite every missing asset to HTML; a script request needs a script, not the home page.','What happens if neither candidate exists?','A 404 response','A new file is created'),
('Use a helpful error page','A custom error page explains a missing route while retaining a useful HTTP status.','error_page 404 /404.html;\nlocation = /404.html {\n  internal;\n}','The configured local 404 page can be used for missing content. internal prevents normal direct external requests to this exact location.','Write a friendly 404 page with a link back to the home page.','Do not return a success status for every missing URL.','Which status means not found?','404','200'),
('Content types matter','A MIME type tells the browser what kind of file it received. Standard Nginx MIME mappings cover common web assets.','http {\n  include mime.types;\n  default_type application/octet-stream;\n}','The mappings help return CSS as text/css and JavaScript with a suitable script content type. The include path depends on the installation.','Explain why a CSS request should not receive text/html.','A wrong content type can stop scripts, styles or WebAssembly from loading.','What does a content type describe?','The kind of response data','The visitor\'s password'),
('Cache deliberate file versions','Caching lets browsers reuse files. Long caching works best for files whose names change when their contents change.','location /assets/ {\n  expires 1h;\n}','This fragment permits a one-hour freshness period for matching responses. The correct policy depends on how the files are versioned.','Compare caching app.abc123.js with an unversioned index.html.','Do not cache a frequently updated HTML page for a year without a plan to refresh it.','Which files suit long caching best?','Files with content-versioned names','Every changing HTML page'),
('Read access and error logs','An access log records requests. An error log records problems such as missing permissions or invalid configuration.','access_log /absolute/practice/logs/access.log;\nerror_log /absolute/practice/logs/error.log warn;','Use writable log paths in a private practice setup. The two logs answer different questions.','Choose which log helps find a file-permission error.','Avoid exposing logs publicly or recording unnecessary sensitive data.','Which log records server problems?','The error log','Only the stylesheet'),
('HTTPS protects the connection','HTTPS uses TLS to encrypt traffic between the browser and server. A certificate identifies the hostname for that connection.','Browser -> encrypted HTTPS connection -> server\nCertificate: must match the intended hostname\nKeys: kept private on the server side','Encryption protects the connection. It does not prove that the site\'s content is honest or bug-free.','Explain why a private key must never be shipped as a public asset.','Do not copy a real private key into a tutorial or public repository.','What must remain private?','The TLS private key','Every public CSS file'),
('Validate before reload','A configuration test can catch syntax problems before the server tries to use a new configuration. Reloading is a separate action.','nginx -t','Run this only for the configuration you are authorised to inspect. A successful syntax test does not prove all site routes work.','List pages and asset types to check after an approved reload.','Do not restart or reload someone else\'s server while practising.','Does a syntax test replace route testing?','No','Yes'),
]
C('nginx','Nginx can deliver static website files. Learn request paths, configuration blocks, content types, caching and error pages by reading small examples for a local practice setup.','These are configuration fragments unless shown as a whole structure. Do not change a system server. A separate local Nginx installation is optional; the tutorial application itself stays static.','https://nginx.org/en/docs/beginners_guide.html',[L(*r,language='text') for r in nginx])

apache=[
('An HTTP server sends responses','Apache HTTP Server accepts web requests and sends responses. For a static site, the response body often comes straight from a file.','Request: GET /club.html\nResponse status: 200 if the file is served\nResponse body: the HTML file','The browser displays the returned HTML. A web server is separate from the browser that runs the page scripts.','Draw the path from a browser request to a static file.','Apache HTTP Server is not the same project as every other tool with Apache in its name.','What does an HTTP server send?','Responses to requests','A mandatory user account'),
('Listen on a practice port','Listen selects the address and port where Apache accepts connections. Bind a local experiment to loopback.','Listen 127.0.0.1:8080','The practice server accepts connections on localhost port 8080 when started with a valid full configuration.','Identify which number is the port.','Do not bind a learning server to every network interface without understanding the exposure.','Which port is selected?','8080','127'),
('Virtual hosts choose a site','A virtual host groups configuration for a site. ServerName identifies the intended host name.','<VirtualHost 127.0.0.1:8080>\n  ServerName localhost\n  DocumentRoot "/absolute/path/to/club-site"\n</VirtualHost>','The block describes a local site and its file root. It is a fragment for an authorised practice configuration.','Find the name and document root in the block.','The first matching virtual host can affect requests with unexpected hostnames; review the whole configuration.','What does DocumentRoot name?','The directory for site files','The browser\'s download folder'),
('Directory access is explicit','A Directory block applies settings to a filesystem directory. Access rules should expose only intended public files.','<Directory "/absolute/path/to/club-site">\n  Require all granted\n  Options -Indexes\n</Directory>','The example allows access to this specific public directory and disables automatic directory listings.','Explain why a private notes directory should not use this public rule.','Never grant public access to an entire home directory just to serve one page.','What does -Indexes prevent?','Automatic directory listings','All file requests'),
('Choose the first page','DirectoryIndex lists candidate files for a directory request. The first existing suitable file can be used.','DirectoryIndex index.html','A visitor opening the directory can receive index.html. The directive does not generate the file.','Write a minimal index.html for a club.','A missing index file is not a reason to expose private directory contents.','Which file is the default here?','index.html','passwords.txt'),
('Understand URL and file paths','A URL path and a filesystem path are different. DocumentRoot usually provides the base used to map a URL path to a file.','DocumentRoot: /srv/club-site\nURL path: /images/logo.png\nMapped file: /srv/club-site/images/logo.png','The mapping joins the public path to the chosen root. Other directives can change this mapping.','Map /style.css using the same root.','Do not let a user choose an arbitrary filesystem path.','What is the mapped logo path?','/srv/club-site/images/logo.png','/images only'),
('MIME types describe files','A MIME type tells the browser what kind of response it is receiving. Apache uses configured mappings and modules for common file types.','CSS: text/css\nJSON: application/json\nHTML: text/html','Each type helps the browser handle the response correctly. Serve an asset with its actual content, not a fallback HTML page.','Match a .css request to the right content type.','A 200 response containing the wrong file type can still break the page.','Which type describes CSS?','text/css','text/html'),
('Modules add features','Apache modules add features such as headers, rewriting or TLS. A directive may require its matching module to be loaded.','Header set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"','This header directive needs mod_headers. It asks browsers not to guess a different type from the supplied content type.','Find the module name in the official header documentation.','Do not assume every Apache installation loads the same modules.','Which module provides Header?','mod_headers','A browser extension'),
('Read htaccess limits','An .htaccess file can apply permitted directory settings when the server allows overrides. It is not always enabled or needed.','Server-level choice: AllowOverride None\nResult: .htaccess overrides are not used for that directory','Using central configuration can be clearer when you control the server. A hosted environment may allow selected overrides instead.','Explain why copying an .htaccess snippet may do nothing on a given host.','Do not enable every override merely to make an unfamiliar snippet work.','Does every host honour .htaccess?','No','Yes'),
('Custom error documents','ErrorDocument can point to a local page that explains a status such as not found.','ErrorDocument 404 /404.html','The server uses the local 404 page for missing content according to its configuration. The file should contain useful navigation.','Write a friendly sentence for a missing lesson page.','Do not make a missing script return the home page with a success status.','Which status is configured?','404','201'),
('Logs explain requests and problems','Apache access logs record request information. Error logs help diagnose server failures or configuration problems.','Access log question: which URL was requested?\nError log question: why could the server not read the file?','The two sources complement one another. Keep log access restricted.','Describe an error message useful without revealing private data.','Do not publish logs as static website files.','Which log is useful for a file read error?','The error log','A quiz score file'),
('Check before changing a server','Validate the configuration before an approved reload, then test real routes and assets. A syntax check does not prove the whole website works.','apachectl -t','On installations providing apachectl, this checks the configured syntax. The exact command name can vary by operating system.','List checks for the home page, a nested route, CSS and a missing page.','Do not reload or stop an organisation\'s server as a learning experiment.','What should follow an approved configuration change?','Route and asset checks','Assuming every URL works'),
]
C('apache','Apache HTTP Server can serve static web pages and assets. Learn virtual hosts, directory access, content types, modules and error pages through simple configuration examples.','Read these examples as configuration fragments. Commands require a separate authorised local Apache installation. No server is added to the learning application.','https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/getting-started.html',[L(*r) for r in apache])
